{"duration_api_ms":7015,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7b873829-c768-4b68-9457-3e6de55a7d8d","total_cost_usd":0.0009052999999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1007,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":570},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":705,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1007,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":705},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1248,"outputTokens":1279,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":705,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0009052999999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":816,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":705,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I can't see the specific AP agreement forms you're referring to, so this is a general answer based on the standard US and Irish structures.\n\n**Rule 6c-11 (US):** The rule is an exemptive framework under the Investment Company Act of 1940 that lets qualifying ETFs operate without individual exemptive orders. It doesn't prescribe AP agreement signatories. Those are set by the fund's contracts. Typically the fund (acting through its trust) and the Authorized Participant are the parties, with the distributor often involved. The AP must be a registered broker-dealer and a DTC participant, and the trust is generally the fund's legal signatory, acting through its trustees.\n\n**Irish ICAV:** An ICAV is a corporate vehicle under the ICAV Act 2015, not a trust. It has its own legal personality and is governed by a board of directors. The ICAV itself, acting through its directors or manager, signs AP agreements. Sub-funds have segregated liability. Regulation is by the Central Bank of Ireland under UCITS rules, not the 1940 Act.\n\n**Key contrast:** US ETFs sign through a trust with trustees, under a 1940 Act framework. Irish ICAV ETFs sign as a corporate body with directors, under UCITS.\n\nFor precise clause-level analysis, please share the forms.","ttft_ms":3294,"type":"result","duration_ms":5432,"uuid":"0c862217-bb57-4830-b942-a4efd96c6b07","ttft_stream_ms":416,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":417,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
